{"term":"cough","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:158c7487f22c595885","definition":"Sometimes followed by up: to force (something) out of the lungs or throat by pushing air from the lungs through the glottis (causing a short, explosive sound), and out through the mouth.","example":"Sometimes she coughed up blood.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["cough down","cougher","coughing","coughingly","cough out","cough over","cough up"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cough#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:767a76103d26ab2da8","definition":"To cause (oneself or something) to be in a certain condition in the manner described in etymology 1 sense 1.1.","example":"He almost coughed himself into a fit.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["cough down","cougher","coughing","coughingly","cough out","cough over","cough up"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cough#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:dc843f7387e71f05a3","definition":"To express (words, etc.) in the manner described in etymology 1 sense 1.1.","example":"No ſtationary ſteeds / Cough their ovvn knell, vvhile heedleſs of the ſound / The ſilent circle fan themſelves, and quake.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["cough down","cougher","coughing","coughingly","cough out","cough over","cough up"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cough#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2a7668abc6f315b231","definition":"To surrender (information); to confess.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, transitive","wordFamily":["cough down","cougher","coughing","coughingly","cough out","cough over","cough up"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cough#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8fc1c4ee350242dc73","definition":"Chiefly followed by up: to give up or hand over (something); especially, to pay up (money).","example":"By the time you get back the men will all be striking out for the fire, and we'll break for the house and collar the dollars. Everybody cough up what matches he's got.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively, slang","register":"figuratively, slang, transitive","wordFamily":["cough down","cougher","coughing","coughingly","cough out","cough over","cough up"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cough#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ad9d588fa12c4a0636","definition":"To push air from the lungs through the glottis (causing a short, explosive sound) and out through the mouth, usually to expel something blocking or irritating the airway.","example":"I breathed in a lungful of smoke by mistake, and started to cough.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["cough down","cougher","coughing","coughingly","cough out","cough over","cough up"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cough#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:230fde9a51cc3a3efd","definition":"To make a noise like a cough.","example":"The engine coughed and sputtered.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransi